description:
In repos/identity-vessel/src/resolvers/issue-key.ts, extract the key-minting body of issueApiKey() into a new exported function named mintApiKey() that performs no authorization check.

The file today contains this exact text (verbatim, occurring once):

  const authz = await authorizeAdmin(authHeader);
  if ('status' in authz) return authz;

  const validated = validateInput(body);

Change ONLY that text to read:

  const authz = await authorizeAdmin(authHeader);
  if ('status' in authz) return authz;

  return mintApiKey(body);
}

/**
 * Mint + persist a key, WITHOUT any authorization check.
 *
 * Split out of issueApiKey() so a caller that has established authority by other
 * means can reuse the exact minting path rather than reimplementing it. The only
 * such caller is the loopback admin-bootstrap resolver, which proves in-container
 * root by presenting API_KEY_SECRET.
 *
 * Anything reachable from the network MUST call issueApiKey() instead. This
 * function grants an arbitrary scope set, including 'admin', to any caller.
 */
export async function mintApiKey(body: unknown): Promise<IssueKeyResult> {
  const validated = validateInput(body);

Everything after that point in the original function is unchanged and becomes the body of mintApiKey — starting at the existing line `  if ('status' in validated) return validated;` and running through the function's existing closing brace. Do not modify any other line, import, or export in the file. issueApiKey must keep its exact current signature and its authorizeAdmin-first behaviour.

This is a pure refactor: no behaviour change for existing callers.

